## Review Guidelines
1. Check for Python-specific issues: type safety, proper exception handling, resource management
2. Look for security vulnerabilities: injection, insecure deserialization, path traversal
3. Evaluate code style compliance (PEP 8), docstrings, and type hints
4. Check for performance issues: unnecessary computations, N+1 queries, memory leaks
5. Severity levels: critical (must fix), warning (should fix), suggestion (nice to have), info (informational)

